The camera wearer is standing immediately beside a clothing rack, with several garments within arm’s reach. A woman is nearby on the opposite side of the rack—roughly one to two metres away—and appears oriented toward the merchandise rather than waiting for a presentation. Neither person is clearly blocking the other’s path. The mannequins and display window are farther away and irrelevant to the immediate interaction.

The most natural next action is to inspect a piece of clothing on the rack. Folding merchandise, checking specifically for damage, or showcasing an item would require evidence of an employee task or active customer engagement that is not visible.

